  <bioghist id="7faa0dd602a878de8da45db94c9fc487">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Ellen Brown is a development finance specialist, entrepreneur, and former program officer at the Ford Foundation. Brown started at the Ford Foundation as a Program Investment Officer in its Program Related Investments Program (PRI) in the late 1980s. Then she moved to the Foundation's South Africa and Namibia Program where she was based as a Program Officer at the Johannesburg, South Africa office. In 1998, she became a Program Officer in the Asset Building and Community Development Program (ASSETS), Economic Development unit. She stayed in that position until she left the Foundation in 2000.</p><p>After leaving the Ford Foundation, Brown worked as Director of Strategic Initiatives at the New Jersey Institute for Social Justice. She later opened her own business, the Doll Loft which sells doll making kits. Brown earned an M.B.A. from Columbia University.</p>  </bioghist>
